+# Registered snapshot skinning subset
+
+`InitSkinnedPositionFromCPSnapshot`, `SnapshotRigidSkinToBones`, and the immutable
+`SnapshotSkinningInput` now connect the previously checked position kernels.
+Each initializer owns its `SnapshotRowCursor`. Only sequential rows, a single
+unit-weight named bone, zero inherited velocity and default copy/normal/radius
+modes are admitted. The rigid operator requires full strength. Missing providers,
+changed binding identities and unsupported variants fail explicitly.
+
+The new particle property travels through the existing collection's current and
+initial arrays. It adds no parallel index map. Rest positions use the existing
+native hitbox-offset attribute; the rigid update reads the literal final initial
+previous position from the corresponding initial array slot. It does not zero,
+subtract, normalize or reinterpret that value. A loop index selects both arrays,
+so this path does not trust a writable particle identity as an array offset.
+
+`SnapshotSkinningRuntime.tla` checks this synchronous spawn/initial-copy/update
+path plus compaction, slot reuse and changed provider identities. Its capacity is
+2, total spawns 3, clears 1, bindings A/B: 218 states, depth 10, all five mutants
+killed. The matrix transform is abstract in the model; code oracles check math.
+`SnapshotRowCursor` separately checks two independent initializer cursors and
+reset/modulo behavior. No new mutable cache or lifecycle is introduced by the
+immutable binding record or the pure position kernels.
+
+The host's `research/ParticleProbe/SnapshotRuntimeInputs.tla` checks explicit
+frame admission, one-frame advances, exact CP/bone queries and completion before
+publishing acknowledgements: ticks 0..1, one supplied key and one wrong key,
+18 states/depth 6, all seven mutants killed. Host JSON parsing, resource/model
+identity and finite rigid-matrix checks are exercised by actual parser tests.
+
+Actual registered classes match 28 eligible native initializer fixtures and
+100 eligible native update fixtures. The older pure kernel oracle still covers
+the broader 84/140 prepared cases, including rigid and missing-matrix behavior
+that this registered subset deliberately refuses. Full simulation exercises
+initial copy, distinct initializer contexts, wrap, replay, removal, compaction
+and reuse. These are synthetic explicit matrix inputs, not a normal exporter
+acquisition proof or a full-scene/render certification.
+
+Live authored crossbow samples independently established nonzero world-like
+InitialPosition == InitialPrevious and 44 particles per snapshot trace. Fitted
+transform consistency is indirect evidence, not independently acquired live bone
+parity. Normal recorded CP0/attachment acquisition, saved-package binding,
+normal moving export and remaining rope shader inputs are unfinished. The normal
+package validator continues to withhold unqualified snapshot-model states.
+
+Simplification: one immutable per-particle binding replaces a proposed side map
+keyed by particle id, eliminating separate prune/reset/reuse bookkeeping. Existing
+arrays carry ownership and initialized attributes together. One root frame
+provider serves children; no child-local pose history or root CP alias is added.
